---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { verifyItems } from '../../data/verify';
const open = verifyItems.filter((v) => v.status === 'open');
const done = verifyItems.filter((v) => v.status === 'verified');
---
<Base
  title="Unverified specs"
  description="Every number on this site that has not yet been checked against a primary source, and what the source is."
>
  <div class="shell railed flow vfy">
    <span class="rail-mark" aria-hidden="true">?</span>
    <h1>What has not been verified</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This site publishes a number in one of two states: sourced, or openly marked as not
      yet sourced. There is no third state where it quietly hopes to be right.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything below is written from working knowledge and has <b>not</b> been checked
      against a primary source. Where any of it appears on the site, it renders as
      <span class="spec">a figure</span>
      <span class="spec-src spec-src--unverified">[unverified — check your manual]</span>
      and links here. Your manual, your chain box, and the standard itself outrank this
      site on every line of this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Open — {open.length} items</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Table, scrolls sideways">
      <table>
        <caption class="sr-only">Unverified specifications and their primary sources</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Where it appears</th><th scope="col">Who is the authority</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {open.map((v) => (
            <tr><td>{v.what}</td><td>{v.where}</td><td>{v.source}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    {done.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Table, scrolls sideways">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{done.map((v) => <tr><td>{v.what}</td><td>{v.where}</td><td>{v.source}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
    <p>
      A safety site that publishes a torque figure it has not checked is worse than one
      that says “check your manual”, because the first one gets believed. Numbers here
      either carry their source or carry a warning — and this page is the list of the
      second kind, in public, so it is visibly a debt rather than quietly a risk.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you have a primary source for any line above,
      <a href="https://github.com/mechaloctopus/chainsaw/issues">open an issue</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .vfy { padding-top: 2rem; }
</style>
